+## Failing scenarios
+
+- **CONSISTENT-WORDS** Import is called Import, and the one-table check-in has one name: undefined
+- **SHARED-DOWNLOADS** the screens that offer a file save it with saveFile: Export, Import’s workbook, Data’s Spreadsheets, Activity, set-up’s template and research notes: undefined
+- **TABLE-LAYOUTS** the AI assistant saves a table layout, lists it and exports the table as that view shows it: undefined
+- **ROUND-TRIP** the same round trip through the AI assistant: export_table, then bulk_change, changes nothing; an edit changes just that: undefined
+- **MCP-FEEDBACK** the MCP server’s list_feedback, get_feedback and update_feedback reach it with any token, on the public key, with the inbox’s rules: undefined
+- **FEEDBACK-RAISED** a sender sees “You raised this” on the entry that fixed their feedback: the database gives a person their own feedback’s statuses only, and What’s new matches by person and id: undefined
+- **MCP-PICTURES** get_markup and review_inbox send any token the markup’s picture as image content, read by its public address; when the bucket isn’t open, they say why: undefined
+- **MCP-PARITY** reviews: set one up, walk its agenda, say things, correct them; only people in it change it: undefined
+- **MCP-PARITY** watching: watch a goal, a tree or a level, list it, stop: undefined
+- **MCP-PARITY** the end of the cycle: wrap-ups open in the last two weeks, by the day; owners wrap up; an admin starts the next cycle: undefined
+- **MODULES** refuses a switched-off module’s AI tool, and runs it when it’s on: undefined
+- **SPREADSHEETS-ON-DATA** has the AI’s export tools in the spreadsheets module: undefined
